  "presentation_summary": [
    "74-year-old Japanese man had 2 months of systemic muscular pain and persistent high CRP despite low-dose prednisolone.",
    "He developed mononeuritis multiplex involving left ulnar and peroneal nerves with sensory loss and left foot drop.",
    "On admission he was afebrile but hypertensive at 178/124 mmHg and had leukocytosis, anemia, thrombocytosis, CRP 19.7 mg/dL, BUN 40 mg/dL, proteinuria, and hematuria.",
    "After methylprednisolone pulse therapy he developed abdominal pain; abdominal X-ray showed paralytic ileus and CT suggested nonocclusive mesenteric ischemia.",
    "Emergency surgery found segmental jejunum-to-ileum ischemia/necrosis over about 2 m; pathology of medium to small arteries confirmed PAN."
  ],
